"text": "If a pie chart's printed percentage labels are treated as the authoritative market-share values, then the brand whose label has the highest numeric value is the current market leader, and the matching public option should be selected.",
"component": "encoding/task relation",
"conditions": "Assumes the printed percentages are valid and comparable; assumes 'market leader' means the largest printed share."
},
{
"id": "r2",
"text": "If the pie chart's visible slice areas are treated as the authoritative market-share values, then the brand whose slice occupies the largest visible area is the current market leader, and the matching public option should be selected.",
"component": "encoding/task relation",
"conditions": "Assumes the drawn slice geometry is valid and comparable; assumes 'market leader' means the largest visible slice."
},
{
"id": "r3",
"text": "If the printed percentage labels and the visible slice areas disagree, the chart is internally inconsistent, and the current market leader is underdetermined until the discrepancy is resolved.",
"component": "scale comparability",
"conditions": "Applies when the highest printed percentage is attached to a slice that is not the largest visible slice."
}
